# Copy to .env and adjust. `pnpm dev` runs the appliance's one mode as a development box (docs/decisions/hermes-engine.md
# HE-49): no licence, the box's identity made at the first start and a stand-in manager under WHOMBAT_HOME, no relay,
# FakeGitHub, the scripted Hermes. For development on your own machine only: the values below are fixed development
# passwords and tokens. When other instances run on this machine, use a free PORT, your own WHOMBAT_HOME and your own
# database.

# Server
# The loopback listener (runner protocol, agents' MCP, the AI gateway relay, the demo's controls). The runner reaches
# it at http://localhost:$PORT; WHOMBAT_SERVER_URL tells it otherwise (then change it together with PORT).
PORT=4400
HOST=127.0.0.1
LOG_LEVEL=info
# The database (docker compose's Postgres on :55432; use a database of your own for throwaway work). The boot
# migrates it outside production.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://whombat:whombat@localhost:55432/whombat
# Whombat's own directory on this machine (default ~/.whombat): the box's identity (identity/content.key), the stand-in
# manager's and the admin socket (manager.sock, admin.sock), workspaces/, files/, credentials/, hermes/.
# WHOMBAT_HOME=~/.whombat
# Encrypts every principal's Ed25519 signing key at rest (AES-256-GCM). 32 random bytes, base64:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# Required in production. Left empty in development, the server falls back to a fixed, publicly known key
# derived from "whombat/dev-master-key/v1" and logs a warning: fine for local data, never for real data.
# Keys encrypted under one master key cannot be decrypted under another, so keep it once you have data.
WHOMBAT_MASTER_KEY=
# The edition (HE-58): `commercial` (the default) or `community` — no licence, control, relay or remote help; claimed on
# the box's own page (http://localhost:<PORT + 80>/, the claim code in the server log), invites and devices by link,
# Web Push and mail from the box, a stand-in Tailscale that signs itself in (docs/decisions/hermes-engine.md HE-S221).
# WHOMBAT_EDITION=community
# The appliance licence: `off` (the default outside production and on a community box) or `on` (a commercial box in
# production, where `off` is refused; a community box refuses `on`).
# WHOMBAT_LICENCE=off
# The hosted UI's origin the server writes links to (default http://localhost:5180 outside production; a community box
# has none: its own page stands for it).
# WHOMBAT_APP_URL=http://localhost:5180
# 1: the demo storyline plays on server start (Dusty's run reaches 41 of 41, Mara approves, the staging deploy goes
# out). The agent's part is the scripted Hermes, `pnpm dev`'s default. Replay or rewind it with `pnpm demo:play` /
# `pnpm demo:reset`.
WHOMBAT_DEMO=0
# The box's own email (invites and notification emails; HE-56). Outside production it defaults to the local Mailpit
# (SMTP :51025, inbox UI http://localhost:58025); in production there is no default; `off` disables it anywhere, and
# lets owners set their own mail server in Settings (`host.mail.set`, HE-S215).
SMTP_URL=smtp://localhost:51025
# Runner token(s), comma-separated; the runner sends the first. Defaults to dev-runner-token outside production.
RUNNER_TOKEN=dev-runner-token

# Hermes Agent runs every turn (HE-01). Unset here and in the environment, `pnpm dev` runs the scripted Hermes
# (packages/agent-runtime/src/hermes/testing/scripted-hermes.ts) with WHOMBAT_ALLOW_SCRIPTED=1, so turns need nobody's
# sign-in. For the real one: `pnpm hermes:install`, then point WHOMBAT_HERMES_BIN at it; its turns run on each person's
# Claude Code or Codex sign-in. The profiles (one HERMES_HOME per person) live in WHOMBAT_HERMES_ROOT.
# WHOMBAT_HERMES_BIN=/path/to/hermes
# WHOMBAT_HERMES_ROOT=~/.whombat/hermes
# 1: a runner whose Hermes is the scripted one (HE-46) runs turns without anyone's sign-in. Never on an appliance.
# WHOMBAT_ALLOW_SCRIPTED=1

# Runner (apps/runner). Every turn runs in its managed sandbox; its task cgroups come from a transient systemd user
# scope on a development host (`systemd-user`, the default); the appliance sets `delegated`.
RUNNER_CONCURRENCY=4
# WHOMBAT_SANDBOX_CGROUP=systemd-user
# Git worktrees for coding work (default $WHOMBAT_HOME/workspaces).
# WHOMBAT_WORKSPACES=

# GitHub (docs/github.md): gh = each burrow's GitHub as the GitHub sign-in of the person who connected it, fake = the
# in-memory FakeGitHub (development, tests, demo), off. auto = gh in production, the fake otherwise.
WHOMBAT_GITHUB=auto
# How often a switched-on repo is read from GitHub while a person is active, ms (0: never on its own); while an
# agent's run, push, deploy or PR checks are live there; and while nothing is (docs/decisions/polling.md PL-01).
# WHOMBAT_GITHUB_POLL_MS=30000
# WHOMBAT_GITHUB_POLL_FAST_MS=10000
# WHOMBAT_GITHUB_POLL_IDLE_MS=180000
# Approved deploys run a workflow_dispatch: one file, or <owner/repo>[:<env>]=<file>,… with * defaults.
# Unset: deploys are simulated (the demo keeps its own).
# GITHUB_DEPLOY_WORKFLOW=deploy.yml
# Failed GitHub Actions jobs an automation's merge runs once more: once (default: every failed job) or infrastructure
# (only a timeout, a lost runner or a failed setup step), for every repo or as <owner/repo>=<value>,… with * defaults.
# WHOMBAT_MERGE_RERUN=AcmeHQ/development=infrastructure
# FakeGitHub keeps real bare repositories here so live agents can clone and push (optional).
# WHOMBAT_FAKE_GITHUB_GIT_ROOT=/tmp/whombat-fake-github

# Google accounts for personal agents (docs/decisions/connectors.md): real = Google's APIs with the OAuth client
# an admin sets up in Settings → Connections, fake = an in-memory mailbox, calendar and drive, off.
# Default: real (fake in tests and the demo).
# WHOMBAT_GOOGLE=real
# The Google OAuth client in config instead of Settings (both or neither; the secret may be a _FILE).
# WHOMBAT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=1234567890-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
# WHOMBAT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=/home/you/.config/whombat/google-client-secret

# Attachments (docs/decisions/bp-attachments.md): where the bytes live (default $WHOMBAT_HOME/files), the largest
# file (bytes, default 250 MiB), how long an unsent upload is kept (hours), uploads per account per hour, and each
# burrow's storage quota (bytes, default 10 GiB).
# WHOMBAT_FILES_DIR=
# WHOMBAT_UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES=262144000
# WHOMBAT_UPLOAD_ORPHAN_HOURS=24
# WHOMBAT_UPLOAD_RATE_PER_HOUR=200
# WHOMBAT_BURROW_QUOTA_BYTES=10737418240

# Whombat Feedback (docs/feedback.md): `on` (default) takes website reports through the encrypted drop once an owner
# creates an integration; `off` withdraws every site card and stops collecting. A development box has no drop.
# WHOMBAT_FEEDBACK=on

# Link previews under messages (docs/decisions/essentials-conversations.md EC-17…EC-22): the server reads the pages
# messages link to (public addresses on ports 80/443 only, 5 s, 512 KB) and shows their title and description. `off`
# never fetches anything; owners can also switch previews off per burrow. Default on (off in tests).
# WHOMBAT_LINK_PREVIEWS=on

# Whombat checks its own way out every minute (docs/decisions/monitoring.md MON-08): its router, name lookups and the
# internet, which it reaches at Whombat's own service and an anycast address (`host:port,host:port` to choose others).
# On in production; a development box and tests never probe unless it is on.
# WHOMBAT_WAY_OUT=off
# WHOMBAT_WAY_OUT_TARGETS=203.0.113.1:443,1.1.1.1:443

# Secrets can come from mode-600 files instead of this file: set <NAME>_FILE for WHOMBAT_MASTER_KEY, RUNNER_TOKEN,
# DATABASE_URL, SMTP_URL, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON, APNS_PRIVATE_KEY, WHOMBAT_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET.
# WHOMBAT_ENV_FILE points the server and the runner at another env file (then this .env is not read).
# WHOMBAT_ENV_FILE=/home/you/.config/whombat/dev.env
